"pnpm dev" to start server
"pnpm survev-setup" does some random stuff
to change map/gamemode go to config.ts
change default gear go to unlockDefs.ts and add your gears code-name (not in game name)

making a skin:
go to "client\public\img", there you will find "loot" and "player" folders
if you want to make your own designs for a skin seen on the player (there are already some you can change the color of) there are 4 things you might want to make
    first, make a base
        you can copy any of the files titled "player-base-x" in the player img folder and edit them
        for all the new files created, end it like the ones already done with "outfitYourOutfit"
    then, a backpack or "player-circle-x"
    next, feet or "player-feet-x"
    finally, hands (same sprite for both) as "player-hands-x"
for the loot image, go to the loot folder, copy one of the "loot-shirt-x" and do the same as before
you are now done with adding files

now, you need to do 3 things
    1:make a SkinDef (traits for a skin)
        go to "shared\defs\gameObjects\outfitDefs.ts, find "const SkinDefs..."
        copy a SkinDef that is relatively similar to what you want to make (you can figure out what each option does)
        change what you want
            tints are what color an image will become if you do one
        if you want you can also make a BaseDef to make many of a similar skin
    2:add your images to the atlas at "client\atlas-builder\defs\loadout.ts"
        make them similar to the ones already there
        your loot image will go with others and player images will go with others too
    3:add your outfit to the lang json file(s) English is "\client\src\en.json"

To unlock your skin as default, go to unlockDefs.ts and add it to the default unlock stuff